      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me check the compile script and working directory setup.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll write an improved version with meaningful variable names, cleaned-up imports, and clearer structure showing what the test is verifying.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`jsonFormat_Shape0`, `jsonFormat_Value0`, etc.) with descriptive names (`emptyFeatures`, `notLenient`, `baseValue`, `mergedValue`, `valueArray`), removes unused imports, and adds inline comments explaining why `mergeAll` returns the same instance (merging a value with itself is a no-op)."
